150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Pneumonia remains a major public health concern, particularly in vulnerable populations such as children, the elderly, and immunocompromised individuals. Early and accurate detection using chest X-rays is crucial but often limited by the availability of expert radiologists. Although deep learning models have shown promise in automating diagnosis, they typically require large labeled datasets and lack the ability to express uncertainty two critical drawbacks in clinical applications.This study presents an uncertainty-aware pneumonia detection framework that combines Vision Transformers \(ViT\) with Monte Carlo \(MC\) Dropout. ViTs effectively capture spatial dependencies in medical images, while MC Dropout enables the model to estimate predictive uncertainty by performing multiple stochastic forward passes during inference. This allows the system to identify ambiguous cases that may require expert review.To enhance data efficiency, the model also integrates an active learning approach that selects uncertain samples for annotation, thereby improving performance with fewer labeled images. Experiments on a public chest X-ray dataset show that the ViT + MC Dropout model achieves 94.1% accuracy, 96.0% sensitivity, and an AUC of 0.98, with improved uncertainty calibration 85% of predictions had over 90% confidence. Additionally, active learning further improves model accuracy using fewer annotations.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
